# Ⅷ. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)
## 8.1 Routine Maintenance Guide
Base Station Cleaning

Ensure that the base station and its power adapter are kept dry and away from liquids at all times to avoid the risk of electric shock.

Follow the steps below to clean the base station:



Cleaning Procedure

1. Unplug the power cable and remove the base station.

2. Use a non-abrasive cloth slightly dampened with water to clean the base station. Do not use any cleaning agents. When cleaning the base station, do not scratch the front panel or disassemble any components.

## 8.2 Common Issues and Solutions
Q1: During calibration, the system cannot find driver_openvr.so, and the following error occurs:

<font style="color:red;">Error loading /home/midea/liuxin/PIKA/pika_ros/install/lib/plugins/driver_openvr.so:</font>

<font style="color:red;">libopenvr_api.so.1: cannot open shared object file: No such file or directory</font>

Solution: Install the dependency:

```plain
sudo apt install libopenvr-dev
```

Then rerun the calibration process.



Q2: During calibration, the terminal freezes and no positioning error is displayed.

```plain
rm ~/.config/libsurvive/config.json
```

Remove the config.json file and rerun the calibration process.



Q3: After calibration, "error failures" is displayed.

This indicates that the calibration has failed. Please check:

● Whether the environment is exposed to sunlight

● Whether there are active infrared light sources nearby

● Whether the base station is properly positioned

● Whether the Sense device is within the base station’s field of view (FOV)

After verifying all the above conditions, rerun the calibration procedure.



Q4: After successful calibration, TF coordinates drift over time.

Check whether:

● The environment is exposed to sunlight

● There are active infrared light sources nearby

● The base station is properly positioned

● The Sense device remains within the base station’s FOV

After checking the above, rerun the calibration procedure.



Q5: After compiling the camera driver, the image can be viewed in realsense-viewer, but ROS launch reports the following error:

<font style="color:red;">/home/name/pika_ros/install/lib/librealsense2_camera.so: undefined symbol:</font>

<font style="color:red;">_ZN20ddynamic_reconfigure19DDynamicReconfigureC1ERKN3ros10NodeHandleE</font>



Cause:

The ros-noetic-ddynamic-reconfigure package installed by default is the latest version. Due to version updates, it is incompatible.



Solution:

A compatible version is provided in the pika_ros/source/ directory:

ros-noetic-ddynamic-reconfigure_0.3.2-1focal.20240913.193805_amd64.deb



Install it using:

```plain
sudo dpkg -i ros-noetic-ddynamic-reconfigure_0.3.2-1focal.20240913.193805_amd64.deb
```



Q6: Base station cannot localize properly.

Check:

● Base station placement

● Power supply

● Whether there is occlusion between PIKA-Sense and Pika-Station

● Whether there are infrared interference sources



Q7: Fisheye camera is disconnected.

Use the Ubuntu built-in camera application (Cheese) to test the fisheye camera.

If no image is available, please contact technical support.



Q8: Stereo camera is disconnected.

Run:

```plain
realsense-viewer
```

Check whether the camera is detected. If not, contact technical support.



Q9: Can pose information be obtained via TF?

For a single Pika system, pose information can be obtained by subscribing to/pika_pose.



Q10: Error: "Failed to call service".

If this error appears alone, no action is required. It indicates that the data collection service has not been started.



Q11: The following error appears:

<img src="https://cdn.nlark.com/yuque/0/2026/png/69344822/1781750313481-b6810724-a162-42ab-bee6-f0b8e038eb79.png" width="2470" title="" crop="0,0,1,1" id="u3590558a" class="ne-image">

This is caused by missing execution permissions for the install directory.

Run:

```plain
chmod 777 -R install/
```



Q12: Error when running bash scripts/start_single_sensor.bash

Possible cause: missing [realsense2_camera(3).zip](https://drive.weixin.qq.com/s?k=AKcACgdBAAgOrfJWmLAXEA5gb3ANM) file.

Place it into the src directory and build using:

<font style="color:#767171;">catkin_make install -DCATKIN_WHITELIST_PACKAGES=""</font>



Q13: The following error occurs:

<img src="https://cdn.nlark.com/yuque/0/2026/png/69344822/1781750337699-f4ac8a18-443b-4d65-b86a-185348b3a864.png" width="796" title="" crop="0,0,1,1" id="u825f3fe0" class="ne-image">

```plain
Traceback (most recent call last):
  File "/home/ppn/miniconda3/envs/tv/lib/python3.8/site-packages/casadi/casadi.py", line 18, in swig_import_helper
    return importlib.import_module(mname)
  File "/home/ppn/miniconda3/envs/tv/lib/python3.8/importlib/__init__.py", line 127, in import_module
