Cause:

This issue occurs because the application incorrectly links against the older C++ standard library provided by the operating system at runtime, instead of the newer version installed in the Conda environment that is compatible with CasADi. As a result, a library version mismatch causes the import to fail.



Solution:

Set the LD_PRELOAD environment variable to force the dynamic linker to load the correct C++ standard library from the Conda environment:

export LD_PRELOAD=/home/<user_name>/miniconda3/envs/pika/lib/libstdc++.so.6

Replace <user_name> with your actual username and ensure that the path matches your local Conda environment.



